# Rust build artifacts
/target
/installer/target
/tools/vm-setup/target

# Editor / OS cruft
*.rs.bk
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Release artifacts — NEVER commit these to git. They bloat the repo history
# and blow past storage quotas. Distribute binaries/tarballs via releases
# (Forgejo/GitHub release attachments), not the git tree.
*.tar.gz
*.tar
*.tgz
*.rmeta
# Compiled installer binaries (any name we've used for a built artifact)
/artix-installer
/installer/artix-installer
bin18*
artix-installer-bin
/versions
# build-iso.sh installs the freshly built binary here on its way into the image.
# It is a build product that happens to sit inside a tracked directory.
/iso-profile/root-overlay/usr/bin/artix-tui-installer

# Cargo.lock is NOT committed.
#
# It was, once. But the Pinnacle config we ship is itself a cargo project that
# gets built ON THE USER'S MACHINE, at first login — and a lockfile frozen at
# packaging time pinned dependency versions that no longer resolved, so
# `cargo build --locked` failed and the session never started. The installer
# now ships no lockfile and passes no --locked; cargo resolves fresh.
Cargo.lock
installer/Cargo.lock

# Container / toolchain cruft that lives beside the source tree in the dev
# environment. None of it belongs in the repository.
.cache/
.config/
.local/
.npm/
.npm-global/
.npmrc
.wget-hsts
uploaded/
prev_backup/
mockbin/

# Локальні налаштування Claude Code. Вони вже ігноруються глобальним
# ~/.config/git/ignore на машині автора — але це властивість МАШИНИ, а не
# репозиторію: коміт з іншого комп'ютера підхопив би їх. Тека нікому, крім
# власника чекауту, не потрібна.
.claude/

# Робоча інструкція для Claude Code — локальна, у репозиторій не публікується.
# Вона їде в тарболах розробки й описує внутрішню кухню, а не продукт.
CLAUDE.md

# Python bytecode from scripts/ (psf-patch.py and friends).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Built ISO images. The build script writes them into iso/ so there is one place
# to look — but a live image is well over a gigabyte, and GitHub refuses any file
# past 100 MB. They are release assets (see scripts/release.sh), never commits.
/iso/*
!/iso/README.md

# The artools workspace: the profile deployed for buildiso, regenerated from
# iso-profile/ on every build. Parts of it end up owned by root (buildiso runs
# under sudo), which is one more reason it is not something git should carry.
/workspace/

# QEMU test drives (scripts/qemu-test.sh). The folder is not in the repository
# at all: it MAKES ITSELF the first time someone runs the installer in a VM, and
# what it holds is tens of gigabytes of disk images with installed test systems
# in them. Nothing here belongs on GitHub, not even a placeholder — a fresh
# checkout has no vm/ until it needs one. What it is and how to steer it is
# documented in scripts/qemu-test.sh's header, which IS in the repository.
/vm/

# Junk a literal-tilde path creates: artools computes USER_HOME as `~name` under
# sudo, and that never expands inside quotes, so a directory actually called
# `~<user>` appears wherever the build ran. scripts/artools-prepare.sh now
# refuses such a path outright, but one already exists in some checkouts and
# must never be committed.
~*/
